 "inference": [
  "Whenever EA states a change and the two stored sources differ, the registry default is the value after the change. Together with the damage cases (L3327, L3339) this supports one rule for the site: where a registry row exists, use its default.",
  "The own value is EA's old number in 4 of 8 cases. In the other 4 it is neither old nor new (HEMP-T inner radius 1.0, rocket radii 4.5 and 7.0), so the own value is stale data and not reliably 'the previous patch'.",
  "Where no registry row exists the own value can still be current: the MBT-LAW's own MaxSpeed 300 and EngineStrength 100 are EA's new values (L3343). And the IGLA's own values are stale with no row to replace them, so 'no row means own is right' does not hold either."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "No in-game reading yet confirms a registry default over an own value; every confirmation so far is an EA statement.",
  "The IGLA and SLM-93A max speed (EA 480) has neither a matching row nor a matching own value (L3343)."
 ],
